# CLAMP copy

- Use short, easy sentences a non technical judge can follow.
- No hyphens in user facing copy. Prefer spaces or rewrite the phrase.
  - Bad: Needs-human, office-supplies, pre-built, on-chain in UI labels
  - Good: Needs human, office supplies, built before the hack, on chain
- Avoid em dashes. Use periods or commas.
- Brand CLAMP as a hero signal on marketing pages. Do not use generic AI SaaS headlines.
- Soft: You set a spending mandate. The agent asked outside it. Nothing paid. The refuse is on the audit trail.
- Technical ids in code may use kebab case when required by routers. User visible labels must not.
